RoboParty standalone Linux adbd

The daemon is built from unmodified AOSP Git submodules plus linux-port.patch.
AOSP source files retain their original copyright and license notices.

The Linux port and CMake source selection adapt work from:
  nmeum/android-tools (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/nmeum/android-tools
  happyme531/standalone-linux-adbd, commit bdb5cdc4b516b3bc71fd2b805bc36190041a9393
  https://github.com/happyme531/standalone-linux-adbd (Apache-2.0)

Contributors to the adapted patches include the Android Open Source Project,
Anatol Pomozov, John Zimmermann, Soren Tempel, meator, Doan Tran Cong Danh,
Biswapriyo Nath, jershell, hallo1, and the android-tools contributors. Original per-file notices
remain in the AOSP sources. This repository independently maintains the
consolidated patch against the pinned AOSP master revision.

The repository's GPL-3.0 license covers the RoboParty build and packaging files.
It does not replace the licenses on AOSP, fmt, or other third-party source files.
